daytona (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Optional log on screen, daytona-greeter: a Windows 98-style dialog for
    greetd with a session chooser, Shut Down and --scale for high-density
    screens.
  * System Properties (General and Performance tabs), from Control Panel,
    My Computer and Win+Pause.
  * Sound events from the freedesktop sound theme, with a Sounds applet.
  * Gradient title bars where the colour scheme sets them; the schemes are
    now Daytona Classic (the default, NT 4.0's solid title bars) and
    Daytona Standard (two-tone, Windows 98 to XP Classic). Settings naming
    the old "Windows Standard" still work.
  * Old X11 (XEmbed) tray icons are shown in the notification area.
  * Never-expiring and critical notification balloons stay open.
  * Lock screen: [Lock] DisableCtrlAltDelete opens straight on Unlock
    Workstation.
  * IBus input methods start the Wayland way in the session.
  * The greeter and Start menu name the operating system, not Daytona.
  * Start menu opens on press with lighter repaints; desktop icons stay
    whole when the scale changes to 200%.
  * Packaging: debian/copyright lists the virtual-pointer protocol file;
    CI runs the smoke tests against the built packages.

 -- Jzume - JZUME <hi@jzu.me>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 17:29:21 +0000

daytona (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Programs from the freedesktop menu files: Start > Programs follows the
    distribution's menu and menu editors, with one program-group icon for
    every folder; StartMenu/FlatPrograms=true in daytona.ini gives NT's
    flat list.
  * NT desktop icons (My Computer, Recycle Bin and ~/Desktop), working
    alongside PCManFM-Qt, which is now the default file manager for
    folders and Start > Find.
  * Date/Time Properties, opened from the clock: date, time, time zone and
    network time.
  * Keyboard Properties with keyboard layouts and the input locale
    indicator.
  * Display Properties arranges monitors, switches one off and chooses the
    primary monitor.
  * Network icon (nm-applet) and fixed tray icon menus.
  * Print Screen and Alt+Print Screen.
  * Programs are asked to close before logging off or shutting down.
  * Portals for file dialogs and screen sharing; D-Bus-started programs get
    the theme.
  * The keyring (Secret Service) starts with the session, and Chromium
    uses it.
  * Only Chicago95's system icons are installed, without the Windows logo;
    desktop icons keep one size on high-density screens.
  * The project moved to JZUME/daytona and jzu.me/daytona, with a new apt
    repository signing key.

 -- Jzume - JZUME <hi@jzu.me>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:07:35 +0000

daytona (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release (pre-release quality) of the Qt edition: the Daytona
    shell, the daytona Qt style, daytona-themetool, the labwc configuration
    and session, and Chicago95 built from its pinned submodule.
  * Taskbar with Start menu, window buttons, notification area (tray icons,
    volume, battery) and clock; notification balloons; desktop with NT
    wallpaper modes plus Fit and Fill.
  * Run, Shut Down (Stand by, Hibernate), Taskbar Properties, Display
    Properties (background, appearance, screen saver, settings) and Mouse
    Properties dialogs, and an NT-style Control Panel.
  * NT-style Workstation Locked screen, Blank Screen screen saver and idle
    lock through swayidle; volume and brightness keys.
  * XDG autostart through dex and LXQt's polkit agent in the session.
  * labwc with a small patch for NT's raised 3D window frames and pressed
    caption buttons, installed privately in /usr/libexec/daytona.

 -- Jzume - JZUME <hi@jzu.me>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:07:50 +0000
